+# Software Factory pages
+
+This folder adds pages to Agent Canvas for spec-driven, governed delivery:
+
+| Page          | Route                        | Reads                                                                                                                           |
+| ------------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Autopilot     | `/autopilot`                 | Start a run from a goal (autonomy, budget); agent server and policy status; recent runs                                         |
+| Autopilot run | `/autopilot/runs/:runId`     | One run: stage lanes, spec and critic, work orders by wave with their attempts, gate checks and findings; pause, resume, cancel |
+| Inbox         | `/inbox`                     | Decisions Autopilot needs from a person (approvals, questions, stuck work), and the history of decisions                        |
+| Requirements  | `/requirements/:changeId?`   | OpenSpec changes: proposal, specs with scenarios, design, tasks                                                                 |
+| Work orders   | `/work-orders/:workOrderId?` | Backlog.md tasks, as a board with a detail panel                                                                                |
+| Audit log     | `/audit-log`                 | The factory's hash-chained audit log                                                                                            |
+
+The data comes from the Software Factory API (`apps/server` in the software-factory
+repo), not from the OpenHands agent server. Vite proxies `/sf-api` to it
+(`SF_API_URL`, default `http://127.0.0.1:4317`). Agents run as ordinary Canvas
+conversations: "Start with an agent" calls `useCreateConversation` with the
+workspace as the working folder and a brief written by the API.
+
+## Files
+
+```
+api.ts                 Typed client for /sf-api
+hooks.ts               React Query hooks, and live updates over Server-Sent Events
+copy.ts                The pages' words (English and Spanish)
+factory-nav-links.tsx  Sidebar entries
+routes/                The pages (requirements, work orders, audit log, autopilot home, run pipeline, inbox)
+components/            Page frame, markdown, badges and state chips, and the plan/approve/start-agent/confirm dialogs
+```
+
+## Outside this folder
+
+Only four upstream files are touched, so pulling new OpenHands releases stays easy:
+
+- `src/routes.ts`: the factory routes
+- `src/components/features/sidebar/sidebar-rail-body.tsx`: `<FactoryNavLinks />`
+- `src/components/features/sidebar/sidebar-nav-link.tsx`: an optional `ariaLabel`
+  prop, so the Inbox entry can say "Inbox, 2 need you" with its count badge
+- `vite.config.ts`: the `/sf-api` proxy
+
+## Rules the pages follow
+
+- Moving a work order to the last status is an approval. Only the Approve dialog
+  does it, and it records who approved and their note.
+- If a work order reaches the last status any other way (an agent ran the
+  Backlog.md CLI, someone edited the file), the API flags it as not approved and
+  the board shows it.
+- Autopilot runs live in the API's run ledger, not in Backlog.md. The pages
+  refetch on the `autopilot.changed` event; the sidebar's Inbox badge also
+  polls `GET /autopilot/inbox/count` every 15 seconds because it shows on
+  every Canvas page.
+- Every Inbox decision is a person's choice recorded in the audit log. Options
+  that end something (cancel, skip) ask for confirmation first, and options
+  that need a note won't go through without one.
+- Strings live in `copy.ts`, not `src/i18n/translation.json`, to keep the
+  factory self-contained. Other Canvas languages fall back to English.
